Hi, Jasmine! Thanks for your interest in the Red Cross Leaders Save Lives project! My name is Amelia and I can be reached at (704) 618-7295.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
Attached are some core documents to review that will be helpful tools to you in getting started. Please review the questions below and let me know if you could provide some feedback by&nbsp;<b><u>Monday March 12th!</u></b><br />
<br />
<b>CHOOSING A LOCATION</b>

<ul>
	<li><font face="arial, sans-serif">What venue could we host the blood drive at? Is there a church, school, or community hall with a large gymnasium, fellowship hall, or conference room that would volunteer their space? Who would we need to reach out to and ask for the space? Usually we need at least 1,000 square feet.&nbsp;</font>

	<ul>
		<li><i><font face="arial, sans-serif">​I have attached our Sponsor Questionnaire&nbsp;that we use to approve spaces!&nbsp;</font></i></li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
<b>RECRUITING DONORS</b>

<ul>
	<li>Who will we be reaching out&nbsp;to recruit donors from? Do you have ideas for groups we can start building a contact list for? Typically, we look to collect about 40 names of potential interested donors before even putting the blood drive on the calendar. Do you feel comfortable doing that initial recruiting?
	<ul>
		<li><i>I have attached a sample outreach email that you may edit to make more personal!</i></li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
<b>THE VOLUNTEERS</b>

<ul>
	<li>Will you have support in the organizing process? Any family members, friends or fellow students willing to volunteer time for recruiting donors via tabling live at church coffee hours or community sports events?&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<b>YOUR COMMITMENT</b>

<ul>
	<li>Do you have a month that ideal to host it? Any sports or activities commitments we need to work around? Family vacations? You will be our #1 volunteer on the day of the blood drive so it&#39;s essential we accommodate your schedule!&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
If you have questions or come up against road blocks -- please reach out to me!<br />
<br />
